#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:69
#: 3c1ce75784b1405fbf391de40894897c
msgid "OSD Panel Item Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:70
#: 84374758f7a74bb487b22f247b4b4b22
msgid "Each OSD panel item uses a set of three variables to be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:72
#: 1483223c21c548d7b5dfd181c8803bda
msgid "``OSDn_<ITEM>_EN`` - activates the respective panel item on screen \"n\" when set to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:73
#: 345321c240cb4ff0aa1121006f7c3bd0
msgid "``OSDn_<ITEM>_X`` and ``OSDn_<ITEM>_Y`` set the horizontal and vertical position of the item, starting with ``X = 0`` and ``Y = 0`` in the upper left corner of your screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:75
#: 8aa64e149515418c9e9fe8e77d6169f6
msgid "the positioning parameters are not used for MSP telemetry only OSDs that create the display only using the telemetry values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:77
#: 4bd35821f25f4e95852b3706a22eae9a
msgid "ArduPilot calculates a sensor-less airspeed estimate that is used if no sensor is present or fails. ARSPD_TYPE must be set to zero in order to display this value as the airspeed item, if no sensor is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:82
#: be5ad1d40336481882c5dc7bef864045
msgid "Display Resolution and Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:83
#: 59997a5c19714680a8e065d8050f7075
msgid "When using DisplayPort, you can select to display either the SD or HD fonts using ``OSDx_TXT_RES`` for each OSD screen enabled. 0 = SD (30x16), 1 = HD (50x18), 3 = HD (60x22)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:85
#: c048593d49c54a88ad1f22e824f2a2a9
msgid "For HDZero you should set ``OSDx_TXT_RES`` to 0 or 1 for each enabled OSD screen. If you set it to 2, the text displayed will be garbled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:87
#: 5f04abbd34874eb988fb6255cf6ef91e
msgid "The SD font's positions are set on a 30x16 X/Y position grid as normal, the HD uses a (1) 50x18 or (2) 60x22 grid. The 50x18 grid has margins at the top/bottom/left/right of the screen before the grid begins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:89
#: 540c080bb1c54823a23afdbfa852799d
msgid "ArduPilot compatible fonts for WTFOS modified DJI goggles can be found `**HERE** <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_OSD/fonts/HDFonts/WTFOS-DJI>`__ ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:91
#: 69900f841b84499db611e54708635a62
msgid "Walksnail/Avatar HD Goggles can select which font they use via a goggle menu. A set of different style fonts that are ArduPilot compatible can be found `**HERE** <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_OSD/fonts/HDFonts/WalkSnail>`__ . The following image shows the font styles included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:97
#: e2577bdf57ba4f9bba2bf62f705ddbfc
msgid "Screens and screen switching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:98
#: dfcf02327def4e73a7e253f90643f24e
msgid "For multiple screen layouts, each screen's \"OSD\" parameter label is trailed by a number, starting with \"1\". For example,  ``OSDn_<ITEM>_x`` is a parameter \"x\" associated with screen 1's \"ITEM\" panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:100
#: e327dd0c63c54219a862f87f54b56446
msgid "multiple screen layout switching is not available on MSP telemetry only OSDs unless the OSD itself provides the capability themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:102
#: f98391fcde064897bc6f5166f791bf6d
msgid "Set ``OSDn_<ITEM>_EN`` =1 to enable screen \"n\" display of this item. This allows one to set individual items active on one screen but have them switched off on another screen. Up to 4 screens are optionally available, and can be individually enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:103
#: f877ea09b9f244f7b163143c1d862195
msgid "Set parameters ``OSDn_CHAN_MIN`` and ``OSDn_CHAN_MAX`` to adjust RC channel pwm limits to use for switching to a respective screen. Be sure to have the ranges non-overlapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:105
#: d1b2a096ae0142e7992ca600d2dd1d40
msgid "There are different switch-method options to meet individual RC systems switch layout requirements. These can be set by parameter: :ref:`OSD_SW_METHOD<OSD_SW_METHOD>`. The options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:108
#: 4c24224c7bbf499599985787cb2c16f5
msgid "0 = switches to next screen if the set RC channel's (:ref:`OSD_CHAN<OSD_CHAN>`) value is changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:109
#: 970bc89ba7ed4d538d584a3adef01eb1
msgid "1 = directly selects a screen based on the set pwm limits for each respective screen. RC channel value must change for new pwm value to be recognized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:110
#: 010a671d5f55491489770cde5e91c9c3
msgid "2 = toggles screens on a low to high transition of set RC channel. keeps toggling to next screen every second while channel value is kept high"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:112
#: 232415922e6e4a5f89bb8448f3a4aacc
msgid "A limitation of telemetry based OSDs is that there's no way for ArduPilot to add new panel items at will, it's the vendor's responsibility to add new features by rolling out new firmware releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:115
#: 525b949407c54532b9261313c77898e4
msgid "Displaying statistics on a dedicated screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:116
#: 150f8feb2c0a42e18045b616de010256
msgid "Displaying statistics on a dedicated screen requires enabling at least one extra screen by setting the respective ``OSDn_ENABLE`` to 1. By default, ArduPilot has only one screen active so in a typical setup one would set (:ref:`OSD2_ENABLE<OSD2_ENABLE>`) = 1 and then enabling the OSD stats panel on screen 2 by setting (:ref:`OSD2_STATS_EN<OSD2_STATS_EN>`) = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:119
#: d2dd360dd85c4c0abe9eaef766a6e1dc
msgid "When the OSD switches to this screen it will check the value of the :ref:`OSD2_STATS_EN<OSD2_STATS_EN>` parameter and if enabled it will override the default behavior of the following OSD items:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:121
#: 454d116eb5304803ae6e87cf9f0ebe70
msgid "OSDn_MESSAGE will display STATS followed by flight time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:122
#: 147a29255fc14962a952b67107c85da3
msgid "OSDn_ALTITUDE will display max altitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:123
#: cdb50661369c49c7a642f1ef2b9ab81e
msgid "OSDn_BAT_VOLT will display min voltage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:124
#: a4c9453432234d6e9e5b7f9f379ffeff
msgid "OSDn_CURRENT will display max current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:125
#: 0fb8516df2b749ac9f811b255f0deda1
msgid "OSDn_GSPEED will display max ground speed (or airspeed if ``OSDn_ASPEED_EN`` is set to 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:126
#: fd6dd2e5dfa3494c97a1d66f7b08a2bd
msgid "OSDn_HOMEDIST will alternates max distance from home and total traveled distance every 2 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-displayport.rst:127
#: d955a85d5f504c79bbcc9c5f52d51e37
msgid "OSDn_RSSI will display min rssi"
msgstr ""

